---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import evidence from "../../public/evidence/manifest.json";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology and Verification"
  description="How Seller Operations Lab separates official marketplace guidance, browser experiments, workflow advice and known limitations."
  activeNav="/methodology/"
>
  <section class="legal-hero legal-shell">
    <h1>Methods and image sources</h1><p>
      Check where a recommendation comes from, what was measured and how to
      reproduce the published examples.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="legal-content legal-shell">
    <h2>Four layers of information</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Official source.</strong> Platform references link to the current
        marketplace documentation and state when it was checked.
      </li><li>
        <strong>Reference measurement.</strong> The downloadable encodings record
        the actual file dimensions, byte counts and hashes from one specified implementation.
      </li><li>
        <strong>Worked example.</strong> Crop geometry and pixel-buffer estimates
        are identified as calculations or controlled examples. They are not device-memory
        or marketplace benchmarks.
      </li><li>
        <strong>Workflow advice.</strong> The guides explain how to make a file decision
        and verify the destination preview. Their recommendations remain separate
        from platform requirements.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <h2>Download and reproduce</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="/experiments/jpg-png-webp/">six-input format comparison</a> publishes
      its normalized inputs and actual output files. It uses two CC0 photographs and
      four clearly identified generated fixtures. The photographs were already JPEG-compressed
      before normalization. Every format starts from the same opaque 1200 × 900 pixels,
      with white compositing; this comparison does not test alpha preservation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Measured {evidence.measuredOn} using Node {evidence.encoder.node}, sharp {
        evidence.encoder.sharp
      } and libvips {evidence.encoder.vips}. JPG/WebP use quality 85 and PNG
      uses default lossless encoding. Equal numeric quality parameters do not
      imply equal perceived quality.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/evidence/manifest.json" download
        >Download the manifest of dimensions, bytes and SHA-256 hashes</a
      >. The <a
        href="https://github.com/huynjuunn-glitch/Milo/blob/main/scripts/generate-evidence.mjs"
        >generator</a
      > and <a
        href="https://github.com/huynjuunn-glitch/Milo/blob/main/scripts/test-evidence.mjs"
        >verification script</a
      > are in the repository. Browser output is a separate test because its decoder,
      scaling and encoder can differ.
    </p>
    <h2>Photograph credits</h2>
    <ul>
      {
        evidence.cases
          .filter((item) => item.credit)
          .map((item) => (
            <li>
              <a href={item.credit!.source}>{item.credit!.title}</a>,{" "}
              {item.credit!.creator},{" "}
              <a href={item.credit!.licenseUrl}>{item.credit!.license}</a>. Used
              as third-party test material; fitted, resized and re-encoded for
              the examples.
            </li>
          ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p>
      Text, pattern, transparency and seeded-noise fixtures are generated test
      images. They are not photographs of goods sold by this project. Synthetic
      stress tests illustrate specific properties and do not establish a
      universal format ranking.
    </p>
    <h2>Revision rules</h2>
    <p>
      Every marketplace reference includes a last-checked date and direct source
      links. We update that date only after reviewing the linked source or
      changing the tested method. A date is not a promise that the platform will
      remain unchanged. When guidance conflicts across official help pages, we
      show the difference rather than inventing one universal threshold.
    </p>
    <h2>Editorial integrity</h2>
    <p>
      We do not invent seller histories, testimonials, user counts, credentials
      or approval results. AI may assist with drafting code or prose, but the
      explanation must be checked against the implemented workflow and cited
      source.
    </p>
    <h2>Technical scope</h2>
    <p>
      Image Prep, Image QA and the format-comparison tool run in the browser.
      Selected files are not sent to a Seller Operations Lab server. Local
      processing still depends on device memory, browser behavior and the user's
      download settings.
    </p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Report a reproducible technical issue or source correction through the <a
        href="/contact/">contact page</a
      >. Do not attach private customer files to a public issue.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
